# Typeahead Search / Combobox (Smooth + Multi-Field)

Use this pattern for admin filter fields that suggest options while typing (Tenant ID, organizations, events, contacts, categories, years, etc.).

**Reference implementation:** [`AdminTenantFilterField.tsx`](mdc:src/app/admin/AdminTenantFilterField.tsx)  
**Server search (name + ID):** [`organizationSelectServerActions.ts`](mdc:src/app/admin/tenant-management/organizations/organizationSelectServerActions.ts)  
**Inspiration:** mosc-temp `YearCombobox` / `CategoryCombobox` (downloads page)

---

## Core Principle: Multi-Field Typeahead (Generic)

Typeahead is **not** a single-column name search. Wherever a user might type an **ID**, **code**, **email**, **domain**, or **display name**, the suggestion query should match **all reasonable identifying fields**—as long as the UX stays smooth (debounced, capped list, merge/dedupe).

| Search UI | Match these fields (examples) |
|-----------|-------------------------------|
| Tenant / org picker | `organizationName`, `tenantId`, `domain` |
| Event picker | title, event id, slug (if present) |
| User / contact picker | firstName, lastName, email, userId |
| Settings / resource lists | display name **and** business key / id |

### Why this matters (Tenant ID fix)

Typing `ten` must surface orgs whose **`tenantId`** contains `ten` (e.g. `tenant_demo_002` / Techies US).  
Typing `techie` must still match **`organizationName`** (“Techies US”).

**Broken:** server only sent `organizationName.contains` → `ten` showed “No matching organizations” even though `tenant_demo_002` exists.  
**Fixed:** parallel criteria, then merge/dedupe:

```typescript
// ✅ DO: searchTenantOrganizationsForSelectServer
const [byName, byTenantId] = await Promise.all([
  fetchTenantOrganizations(page, { search: trimmed, ...sort }),           // organizationName.contains
  fetchTenantOrganizations(page, { tenantIdContains: trimmed, ...sort }), // tenantId.contains
]);
return mergeOrganizationsByKey(byTenantId.data, byName.data).slice(0, LIMIT);
```

- Add `tenantIdContains` → `tenantId.contains` in [`fetchTenantOrganizations`](mdc:src/app/admin/tenant-management/organizations/ApiServerActions.ts) / [`TenantOrganizationFilters`](mdc:src/app/admin/tenant-management/types.ts).
- Client local filter should also match name **and** id (and domain when available).
- After server returns, **merge** with local matches so an empty name-only response never blanks good ID hits already in cache.

Apply the **same idea** to any new typeahead: identify the human label fields + stable id/key fields, query both (or filter both client-side when the dataset is small), merge, cap (~20).

---

## Required Behaviors (Smoothness)

1. **Local controlled input** — Keep `inputValue` in component state. Do **not** drive the input solely from URL/`router` on every keystroke (flicker / list refetch thrash).
2. **Do not write partial typeahead text into the URL** — Typing filters the dropdown only. Commit `?tenant=` (or similar) **only** on suggestion select, Enter, or clear. Debouncing partial strings into the URL causes wrong filters and effect loops.
3. **Multi-field server (and local) match** — See Core Principle above. Never ship a typeahead that only searches the pretty name when users also know the id/code.
4. **`onMouseDown` + `preventDefault` on options** — So input `blur` does not close the menu before `click` runs.
5. **Click-outside closes** — `mousedown` on `document`; ignore events inside the container `ref`.
6. **Keyboard** — `Enter` selects the only filtered match (or commits typed value); `Escape` closes; optionally `ArrowDown` opens.
7. **ARIA** — `role="combobox"`; `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, `aria-autocomplete="list"`; list `role="listbox"` / `role="option"`. Prefer `useId()` for listbox ids; keep stable product ids (e.g. `admin-filter-tenant-id`) when tests/docs reference them.
8. **Clear control** — Clear button uses `onMouseDown={(e) => e.preventDefault()}`.
9. **Resolve URL → label once** — Hydrating a label from a committed id: guard with `resolveAttemptedRef`; accept **exact id matches only** (never `results[0]`). Do **not** put the growing suggestion cache in that effect’s deps in a way that re-fires the same search (infinite loop).

